play (TFT-LCD) panels in South Korea, China, the rest of Asia, North America, and Europe. The company offers display panels for televisions; monitors; IT products comprising notebook computers, desktop monitors, and tablet computers; laptops; smartphones and smartwatches; mobile phones and watches; automobiles; and other products with display devices. It also engages in the operation and management of welfare facilities; management of intellectual properties; production and sale of LCD modules and monitor sets; and investment in venture businesses and technologies. The company exports its products. The company was formerly known as LG.Philips LCD CO., Ltd. and changed its name to LG Display Co., Ltd. in March 2008. LG Display Co., Ltd. was incorporated in 1985 and is headquartered in Seoul, South Korea.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Chul-Dong  Jeong | CEO, President & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 53K people. Each employee generates $47K of free cash flow annually.","financial_summary":["LG Display Co, Ltd AMERICAN DEP is a mid-cap technology business with a $2.5B market cap.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 11% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $2.5B in free cash flow, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage runs at 5.6\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Gross margin trails most Technology peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 76% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"LG Display (NYSE:LPL) Reaches New 1-Year Low \u2013 Here\u2019s What Happened","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/lg-display-nyselpl-reaches-new-1-year-low-heres-what-happened.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793906592.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"LG Display (LPL) vs. Its Competitors Head to Head Analysis","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/01/lg-display-lpl-vs-its-competitors-head-to-head-analysis.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793578494.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.754,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"LG Display (NYSE:LPL) vs. Zebra Technologies (NASDAQ:ZBRA) Critical Survey","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonli